# Dashboard UI

KameOps is **dashboard-first** (no large public marketing surface in v1). Guest-facing or embeddable UIs may come later for specific modules.

## Layout

- Use `(dashboard)` route group with sidebar + header
- Semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`
- Support light and dark mode on every new screen

## Module Pages

| Module | Primary UX |
| ------ | ---------- |
| Overview | Cards: upcoming dues, last SOA run, automation health |
| Credit cards | Table of cards, SOA history, run SOA action, due status |
| Reminders | List/filter reminders, window config, sent log |
| Automations | Job list, cron schedule editor, run history |
| Integrations | Connect Gmail/Telegram/Slack/Calendar with status |
| Receipts | Upload gallery, OCR result, link to mark paid |
| Settings | Profile, timezone, notification defaults |

## Data Tables

Use TanStack Table v8 via shared `DataTable` patterns. Credit card and reminder lists should support sort, filter, and row actions.

## Actions & Destructive Flows

- Confirm before deleting cards or disconnecting integrations
- SOA run: show progress states (searching Gmail, parsing, notifying)
- Mark paid: optimistic UI optional; always show server error messages

## Empty States

- One short title + optional single line + CTA — no essays unless user requests copy
- Link to settings only when the action truly requires configuration elsewhere

## Do Not

- Add unsolicited descriptions, helper paragraphs, or `CardDescription` prose (see `21-minimal-ui-copy.mdc`)
- Put SOA parsing logic in components—call tRPC mutations that invoke services
- Hardcode bank list in UI—load from server constants or DB
